ievements","Steam Cloud","Steam Trading Cards","Family Sharing"],"platforms":{"windows":true,"mac":true,"linux":true},"controller":"full","dev":["Goblinz Studio"],"pub":["Goblinz Publishing"],"released":"Apr 29, 2021","meta":76,"langs":["English","French","Italian","German","Simplified Chinese","Spanish - Latin America","Portuguese - Brazil","Spanish - Spain","Polish","Russian","Japanese","Korean","Traditional Chinese","Turkish","Czech"],"min":[["OS","Windows 7"],["Processor","Core i3 or equivalent"],["Memory","2 GB RAM"],["Graphics","DirectX 11 and/or OpenGL 3.3 compatible video card"],["Storage","1 GB available space"],["Sound Card","Any"]],"rec":[["OS","Windows 10"],["Processor","Core i5 or equivalent"],["Memory","4 GB RAM"],["Graphics","DirectX 11 and/or OpenGL 3.3 compatible video card"],["Storage","1 GB available space"],["Sound Card","Any"]],"deck":2,"blurb":"Dungeon-crawling is flipped around here: you work for the Dungeons Company and defend its treasures from invading adventurers who call themselves heroes. The game alternates between management, where you hire monsters, deal with staff problems such as strikes and keep traps in stock, and dungeon defense, where you study each party's stats and resistances and set up the most suitable traps and monsters against them.\n\nRuns follow a roguelite structure, so each attempt differs, though some bonuses from your Master carry over. The office-comedy framing keeps the tone light. It is single-player with full controller support, suited to strategy fans who enjoy puzzle-like defense planning."}}